1.6.3: Unknown keys are ignored with a warning. A value set here applies only after the next reload. This section is kept for historical reasons and may be removed in a later revision.

0.11.20: Every entry is validated before it is written. Operators should not edit generated files by hand. Unknown keys are ignored with a warning.

4.1.20: The reader tolerates trailing whitespace. Every entry is validated before it is written. The default is deliberately conservative.

2.8.18: This section is kept for historical reasons and may be removed in a later revision. The default is deliberately conservative. Unknown keys are ignored with a warning.

3.3.7: Retries are bounded and jittered. Keys are compared case-sensitively. The service keeps its state in an append-only journal and rebuilds the index on start.

1.9.10: A value set here applies only after the next reload. The reader tolerates trailing whitespace. See the runbook for the rollout procedure.
